      "setReleaseDate": "2016/05/02",
      "whyItBelongs": "Snorlax is rolling through a sunlit town fast asleep, curled into a huge round ball with its eyes shut and a dust cloud trailing behind it. A crowd of startled townspeople is scattering out of the way, with one man mid-leap and a couple of others looking alarmed, while on the right a woman seems to be calmly holding up her phone to take a photo. This is a very different kind of nap from the rest of the Snorlax cards: it’s the only one causing a stampede. The painted, slightly storybook style makes it funnier, since everyone is panicking over an unstoppable sleeper.\n\nThe card is all about this scene. Toss and Turn can be used even while Snorlax is Asleep, and if it is, the attack does 90 more damage. That’s the sleep-rolling you see in the artwork, where being asleep is what makes it so dangerous.",
